// VoxelOceanSurf.ush - The surf (Design/OceanWaves.md section 6; stage O9a). Shared subset
// (VoxelShaderCompat.h): the wave hook (VoxelOceanWaves.ush) and the CPU model
// (VoxelOceanWavesFFT.cpp) add the same surf with this same code.
//
// WHAT IT IS. Near a coast the FFT's long bands (the swell and the long wind sea) hand their
// energy over to surf trains: waves whose crests follow the depth's contours, that shorten and
// slow as the water shallows, steepen into bores as they break, and run up the beach as swash.
// The short bands stay (shoaled and capped, VoxelOceanShoal.ush). Everything is a function of the
// point's depth d (the terrain's, as the mesh, the probe or the query carry it), the shore
// field's beach slope m, landward direction e and distance, the point's sea state, its
// planet-frame position (for the sets' noise) and the ocean clock: deterministic, as the rest of
// the waves.
//
// THE TRAINS. The clock is taken modulo VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP seconds; a train's period is
// WRAP / n with n a whole multiple of VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_GROUP (VoxelOceanSurfCycles), so its phase
// and its groups' phase are exact across the wrap, and the same everywhere (a period that varied
// from place to place would shear the crests as the clock runs). The sea state's peak period
// (0.75 U s, U the larger of wind and swell) falls between two of the trains, which share its
// energy by its place between them (in log period u: amplitudes cos and sin of u pi / 2).
//
// THE PHASE of a train of deep wavenumber k (omega^2 / g) at depth d > 0, the beach taken as
// uniform at the field's slope m (as the O8 warp), measured from the shoreline:
//   theta = Phi(d) + omega t,   Phi(d) = (Y + G(0) - G(Y)) / m,   Y = k d,
// G as VoxelOceanShoal.ush's (G(0) = pi^2 / 8). So d Phi / d s = k r along the distance s = d / m:
// the local wavenumber is the shallow one, the crests move at the shallow-water speed and bunch
// up toward the beach, along the depth's contours (refraction's look), and Phi(0) = 0 (the slope
// changes the phase only as far out as the waves reach, not at the shoreline).
//
// THE WAVE at d > 0: a deep-water height H0 = Hs / sqrt 2 (the long bands' root-mean-square wave
// height: a train of it carries the energy the long bands hand over; the sets' factors on top)
// shoaled by Ks = sqrt(r / 2n) (capped at 2), held under Index x d smoothly (as the FFT's cap):
// Hc. Index = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_INNER x Breaking (0.55 at the default 0.78): a broken wave's
// height in the surf zone is about half the depth (bores run at 0.5 to 0.6; 0.78 is a single
// wave's at the moment it breaks). Its profile (VoxelOceanSurfProfileOf) runs from the crest
// down the back to the trough over 1 - F of the period and back up the front over F, half a
// cosine each (C1, its mean the still level): F one half is a cosine; as the wave saturates
// (H / Index d past 0.4) F falls to (1 - Skew) / 2, a bore whose front is (1 - F) / F times as
// steep as its back. F is held above what the mesh spacing (the height: VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MESH_FRONT
// spacings) or the pixel footprint (the gradient: 2) resolves: the mesh keeps a front it can carry
// without a sawtooth, the normals the sharp one.
//
// THE SWASH: the shoreline's level by Stockdon et al. (2006), as a mean and swings with the
// variance of theirs (their S is a significant swash height, 4 sigma: a swing of amplitude
// sqrt 2 sigma = S sqrt 2 / 4 has its variance; their R2 = 1.1 (setup + S / 2) is the 2% run-up,
// not the typical one):
//   zeta = setup + q (A_inc f(theta0 - lag) + A_ig cos(group phase)),
//   setup = 0.35 b sqrt(H0 L0), A_inc = (sqrt 2 / 4) 0.75 b sqrt(H0 L0), A_ig = (sqrt 2 / 4) 0.06 sqrt(H0 L0)
// (b the beach slope held under 0.1, L0 = g T^2 / 2 pi, H0 the deep significant height; held under
// 0.3, 0.5 and 0.32 H0): the incident swash rides each bore (f the profile with a quick uprush,
// F 0.35, starting as the bore's crest reaches the shoreline: lag = 2 pi 0.35), the infragravity
// swash (most of it on a gentle beach) rides the groups. q holds the swings within SwashReach
// metres of the mean up and down the beach (at the beach's slope b: within SwashReach x b of
// height, smoothly: q = 1 / (1 + (A / (SwashReach b))^4)^(1/4), A the two swings' sum): the
// infragravity swash doesn't shrink with the slope, so on a gentle beach it would sweep tens of
// metres. b, here, in Stockdon's terms and in the blend's width, is the bed's slope (stage O9b3;
// held above a twentieth of the field's), so on a flat the swash hardly moves. Above the still level (d <= 0) the water is that level, flat:
// the terrain hides it where it stands higher, so the waterline climbs the beach and falls back
// below the still level in the backwash (the wet sand shows). Within Dsw of depth (half the
// waves' wavelength at the swash's depth along the beach, so the last bore runs into it) the
// sea's surface (the wave and the surf zone's setup) blends into it. It fades out past 1.5 km
// inland by the field's distance (on both sides of the still level: stage O9b3), and with the
// field's agreement (no swash between two coasts). On land the sheet reaches only 1.5 to 3 times
// SwashReach up the beach from the still waterline (the ground's height over the bed's slope:
// stage O9b3), so a plain near sea level isn't covered by it.
//
// THE SETS: per wave a group factor 1 + 0.4 Sets cos(group phase), the group phase theta / GROUP
// plus a 1.6 km noise (groups of GROUP waves, shifted along the coast), a 410 m noise drifting
// over 2 minutes on the heights (up to 30% either way), and a 610 m noise on the phase (up to half
// a period either way):
// the coast doesn't break all at once. The noises' point comes as whole units of 4096 cm and the
// rest (cm): the waves' reference point's own split (W.RefHigh, W.RefLow) plus the offset from it,
// so the noise is exact to a fraction of a millimetre anywhere on the planet (a float position
// resolves 8 cm there, and a bore's front would show the noise's steps). The cells are whole
// units (10, 15 and 40), so the lattice follows from the units by integer division.
//
// THE HANDOVER: within max(Handover x Hs / Breaking, 2 m) of depth (Hs the long bands'
// significant height) the surf takes the long bands' energy: the trains' amplitude w = 1 -
// smoothstep(0.4, 1, d / that depth), times the field's agreement (|e|^2: between two coasts the
// surf fades, as the warp); the long bands keep sqrt(1 - t^2) (VoxelOceanShoalSettings::LongKeep,
// before the FFT's breaking cap), t the part of w the trains show (stage O9b3: w by the bed's hold
// and by how far the mesh resolves them, by energy): energy the trains can't show stays with the
// long bands, so no band of calm opens where they're too short to draw. Both C1 at the
// handover's edge.
//
// FOAM (stage O9b): a bore makes white water on its face and leaves a trail behind its crest,
// e^(-u / 0.25) over the cycle u since the crest passed (VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_TRAIL; shifted to
// nothing at the trough, where the face's begins), on a carpet of a quarter of it, all times its
// saturation (H / Index d past 0.4); where the footprint doesn't resolve the wave, the pattern
// fades to its cycle's mean (VoxelOceanSurfResolved: no stripes far away); the swash's sheet
// is foamy where it runs thin (its thickness, the level less the bed: e^(-h / 6 cm)) and a fifth
// foam over the rest. Times Foam (the settings' surf foam); the open sea's foam is
// VoxelOceanFoam.ush's.
//
// GRADIENT: the surf is a function of d, so its gradient is d eta / d d times the depth's
// gradient, taken as -m e (the field's slope toward the coast); the noises' gradients and the
// gain's are left out. RESOLUTION: a train's wave is weighed by how well the mesh spacing (the
// height: VoxelOceanSurfMeshResolved, fully from 8 spacings a wavelength, nothing under 4) or the
// pixel footprint (the gradient: VoxelOceanResolved's rule, fully from 4) resolves its local
// wavelength, so a wave too short for the mesh moves the normals only; the swash and the setup
// are levels and stay.
//
// THE DEPTH (stage O9b2): the depth the waves feel is the terrain's with features narrower than
// about twice the shore's depth footprint left out (VoxelOceanPage.usf): the phase turns by
// k r / m radians per metre of depth (10 per metre at 1:50 for a 10 s wave a metre deep), so
// the terrain's fine detail would scatter neighbouring vertices to unrelated phases.
//
// THE BED (stage O9b2): the phase spaces the crests by the field's slope m, but the depth falls
// landward at the bed's own slope b (the smoothed bottom's, BedSlope; m where unknown): on the
// ground the waves are m / b times their local wavelength. That length (Ground) is what the
// mesh and the footprint resolve and what the fronts are held to, and b (held within 2 either
// way) is the depth's gradient the surf's own gradient follows. Where the bottom is much flatter
// than m (b / m under 0.35, none under 0.05) or rises seaward (behind a bar), the phase would
// stall or run backward: the trains fade out there, and the long bands take their energy back
// (stage O9b3: holding it back left calm patches). The swash takes the bed's slope too (stage
// O9b3), so its level follows the beach it runs up.
//
// Lengths: m; the clock: s (wrapped).

#ifndef VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_USH
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_USH

#ifndef VOXEL_FUNC
#define VOXEL_FUNC
#endif

// Include after VoxelOceanShoal.ush.

#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP 3600.0f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_GROUP 6
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TRAINS 8
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI 3.14159265f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI 6.28318531f
// Above this height over the still level (m) no surf (inland, and the basins' land depth).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_LAND 100.0f
// The shortest and longest periods (s): WRAP / 720 and WRAP / 204.
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MIN_PERIOD 5.0f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MAX_PERIOD 17.647059f
// The peak period per speed (s per m/s): sqrt(2 pi 0.8796 / g), VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_PEAK_LENGTH's.
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PERIOD_PER_SPEED 0.75071f
// G(0) = pi^2 / 8.
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_G0 1.2337006f
// The swash: its front's share of the cycle (the uprush), its lag behind the bore's crest at the
// shoreline (rad: the uprush starts as the crest arrives).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWASH_FRONT 0.35f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWASH_LAG 2.1991149f
// The bore's foam trail behind its crest (of the cycle), the swash's foamy thickness (m).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_TRAIL 0.25f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_THIN 0.06f
// The groups' weight per Sets; the heights' drift along the coast per Sets (either way).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_GROUP_WEIGHT 0.4f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRIFT 0.3f
// The trains' deep height per significant height (root mean square: the long bands' energy).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_RMS 0.70710678f
// The bores' height index per breaking index (a broken wave's height over the depth).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_INNER 0.7f
// A swing's amplitude per significant swash height (sqrt 2 / 4: the same variance).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWING 0.35355339f
// The mesh: the least front, in spacings, the height keeps.
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MESH_FRONT 4.0f
// The bed (stage O9b2): slopes above this are known (VOXEL_OCEAN_BED_UNKNOWN below); the trains
// fade out as the bed's slope falls from FADE1 to FADE0 of the field's; the slope is held within
// MAX either way.
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_KNOWN (-1000.0f)
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_FADE0 0.05f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_FADE1 0.35f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_MAX 2.0f
// The handover's least depth (m; past the blend into the swash's level, at most 2 m).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MIN_REACH 2.0f
// The swash fades out inland by the field's distance (m).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_INLAND 1500.0f
// The swash's sheet reaches up the beach this many times its reach, fading out by the second
// (stage O9b3).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SHEET0 1.5f
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SHEET1 3.0f
// The noises' unit (cm): the reference's split (VoxelOceanCharts.h, SplitHigh).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_UNIT 4096.0f

// Train I's cycles per wrap (periods 5, 6, 7.5, 9.1, 10.7, 12.5, 15 and 17.6 s), multiples of the
// group (6).
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfCycles(int I)
{
    return I == 0 ? 720.0f : (I == 1 ? 600.0f : (I == 2 ? 480.0f : (I == 3 ? 396.0f : (I == 4 ? 336.0f : (I == 5 ? 288.0f : (I == 6 ? 240.0f : 204.0f))))));
}

VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfFrac(float X)
{
    return X - floor(X);
}

// An angle brought into [0, 2 pi) (the GPU's sin and cos lose accuracy far from 0).
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfAngle(float A)
{
    return VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * VoxelOceanSurfFrac(A * (1.0f / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI));
}

// A 32-bit hash of a lattice point and a seed, to [0, 1).
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfHash(int X, int Y, int Z, uint Seed)
{
    uint H = (asuint(X) * 0x8da6b343u) ^ (asuint(Y) * 0xd8163841u) ^ (asuint(Z) * 0xcb1ab31fu) ^ (Seed * 0x165667b1u);
    H ^= H >> 15u;
    H *= 0x2c1b3c6du;
    H ^= H >> 12u;
    H *= 0x297a2d39u;
    H ^= H >> 15u;
    return float(H >> 8u) * (1.0f / 16777216.0f);
}

// A lattice coordinate along one axis: Units whole units and Low cm, in cells of Cell units.
struct FVoxelOceanSurfLattice
{
    int Index;
    float Frac;
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurfLattice VoxelOceanSurfLatticeOf(int Units, float Low, int Cell)
{
    // Floor division (the units may be negative).
    const int Q = Units >= 0 ? Units / Cell : -((Cell - 1 - Units) / Cell);
    const int R = Units - Q * Cell;
    const float P = (float(R) * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_UNIT + Low) / (float(Cell) * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_UNIT);
    const float F = floor(P);
    FVoxelOceanSurfLattice L;
    L.Index = Q + int(F);
    L.Frac = P - F;
    return L;
}

// Value noise in [0, 1] at the point (Units whole units, Low cm) in cells of Cell units, smooth
// (cubic weights), for two seeds at once (x and y; the lattice shared).
VOXEL_FUNC float2 VoxelOceanSurfNoise2(int3 Units, float3 Low, int Cell, uint Seed0, uint Seed1)
{
    const FVoxelOceanSurfLattice LX = VoxelOceanSurfLatticeOf(Units.x, Low.x, Cell);
    const FVoxelOceanSurfLattice LY = VoxelOceanSurfLatticeOf(Units.y, Low.y, Cell);
    const FVoxelOceanSurfLattice LZ = VoxelOceanSurfLatticeOf(Units.z, Low.z, Cell);
    const int X = LX.Index;
    const int Y = LY.Index;
    const int Z = LZ.Index;
    const float U = smoothstep(0.0f, 1.0f, LX.Frac);
    const float V = smoothstep(0.0f, 1.0f, LY.Frac);
    const float W = smoothstep(0.0f, 1.0f, LZ.Frac);
    float Out0 = 0.0f;
    float Out1 = 0.0f;
    for (int K = 0; K < 2; K++)
    {
        const uint Seed = K == 0 ? Seed0 : Seed1;
        const float A = lerp(VoxelOceanSurfHash(X, Y, Z, Seed), VoxelOceanSurfHash(X + 1, Y, Z, Seed), U);
        const float B = lerp(VoxelOceanSurfHash(X, Y + 1, Z, Seed), VoxelOceanSurfHash(X + 1, Y + 1, Z, Seed), U);
        const float C = lerp(VoxelOceanSurfHash(X, Y, Z + 1, Seed), VoxelOceanSurfHash(X + 1, Y, Z + 1, Seed), U);
        const float D = lerp(VoxelOceanSurfHash(X, Y + 1, Z + 1, Seed), VoxelOceanSurfHash(X + 1, Y + 1, Z + 1, Seed), U);
        const float N = lerp(lerp(A, B, V), lerp(C, D, V), W);
        if (K == 0) Out0 = N;
        else Out1 = N;
    }
    return float2(Out0, Out1);
}

// The same, drifting in time: T the clock in cells (T >= 0), Cells cells per wrap (the last
// joined to the first). x the noise, y its derivative in T.
VOXEL_FUNC float2 VoxelOceanSurfNoiseTime(int3 Units, float3 Low, int Cell, float T, uint Cells, uint Seed)
{
    const float FT = floor(T);
    const uint C0 = uint(FT) % Cells;
    const uint C1 = (C0 + 1u) % Cells;
    const float X = T - FT;
    const float U = X * X * (3.0f - 2.0f * X);
    const float2 N = VoxelOceanSurfNoise2(Units, Low, Cell, Seed + C0 * 7919u, Seed + C1 * 7919u);
    return float2(N.x + (N.y - N.x) * U, (N.y - N.x) * 6.0f * X * (1.0f - X));
}

// The profile at phase Theta (a crest at 0 mod 2 pi): the back from the crest to the trough over
// 1 - Front of the cycle, the front back up over Front, half a cosine each; its derivatives in
// Theta and in Front.
struct FVoxelOceanSurfProfile
{
    float Shape;        // -1 to 1, mean 0
    float DTheta;
    float DFront;
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurfProfile VoxelOceanSurfProfileOf(float Theta, float Front)
{
    FVoxelOceanSurfProfile P;
    const float U = VoxelOceanSurfFrac(Theta * (1.0f / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI));
    const float Back = 1.0f - Front;
    if (U < Back)
    {
        const float A = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI * U / Back;
        const float S = sin(A);
        P.Shape = cos(A);
        P.DTheta = -S / (2.0f * Back);
        P.DFront = -S * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI * U / (Back * Back);
    }
    else
    {
        const float V = 1.0f - U;
        const float A = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI * V / Front;
        const float S = sin(A);
        P.Shape = cos(A);
        P.DTheta = S / (2.0f * Front);
        P.DFront = S * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI * V / (Front * Front);
    }
    return P;
}

// The settings, as the shaders get them (the chart table's constants, rows 15 and 16, written
// with the shore frame by the surface; FVoxelOceanWaveShaderParams::Surf): Row0 = (strength, sets,
// swash, skew), Row1 = (handover, surf foam, open foam, swash reach m). Breaking: the shoaling's
// breaking index.
struct FVoxelOceanSurfSettings
{
    float Strength;     // 0: no surf
    float Sets;
    float Swash;
    float Skew;
    float Handover;
    float Breaking;
    float Foam;         // the surf's foam (stage O9b; 0 none)
    float OpenFoam;     // the open sea's foam coverage (stage O9b, VoxelOceanFoam.ush; 0 none)
    float SwashReach;   // the swash's swings held within this up and down the beach (m; 0 no limit; stage O9b2)
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurfSettings VoxelOceanSurfSettingsOf(float4 Row0, float4 Row1, float Breaking)
{
    FVoxelOceanSurfSettings S;
    S.Strength = max(Row0.x, 0.0f);
    S.Sets = saturate(Row0.y);
    S.Swash = max(Row0.z, 0.0f);
    S.Skew = clamp(Row0.w, 0.0f, 0.95f);
    S.Handover = max(Row1.x, 1.0f);
    S.Breaking = Breaking;
    S.Foam = max(Row1.y, 0.0f);
    S.OpenFoam = max(Row1.z, 0.0f);
    S.SwashReach = max(Row1.w, 0.0f);
    return S;
}

// The highest the surf can stand above the still level (m) for the long bands' significant height
// Hs: the drift's and the groups' most; the swash by Stockdon's terms at the steepest slope they
// take (0.1) and the longest period, within their caps (the reach's hold left out); a crest at
// the cap with a gain of 1.6.
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfMaxHeight(float Hs, FVoxelOceanSurfSettings S)
{
    if (S.Strength <= 0.0f || S.Breaking <= 0.0f) return 0.0f;
    const float Most = Hs * S.Strength * (1.0f + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRIFT * S.Sets);
    const float Grouped = 1.0f + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_GROUP_WEIGHT * S.Sets;
    const float L0 = VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_GRAVITY * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MAX_PERIOD * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MAX_PERIOD / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI;
    const float Root = sqrt(Most * L0);
    const float Setup = S.Swash * min(0.35f * 0.1f * Root, 0.3f * Most);
    const float Incident = S.Swash * min(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWING * 0.75f * 0.1f * sqrt(Grouped) * Root, 0.5f * Grouped * Most);
    const float Infragravity = S.Swash * min(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWING * 0.06f * Root, 0.32f * Most);
    const float Crest = Setup + 0.5f * 0.84f * 1.6f * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_RMS * Grouped * Most;
    return max(Setup + Incident + Infragravity, Crest);
}

// A point's surf inputs.
struct FVoxelOceanSurfInput
{
    float DepthM;       // the terrain's depth (m, below 0 on land; 1e20 or more unknown)
    float Slope;        // the field's beach slope (held above the least slope)
    float Agree;        // the field's direction's squared length (0 to 1)
    float ShoreM;       // the field's distance (m, below 0 on land)
    float Hs;           // the long bands' deep-water significant height (m)
    float Speed;        // the larger of the wind and the swell (m/s)
    int3 Units;         // the point in the planet frame, for the noises: whole units of 4096 cm
    float3 Low;         // and the rest (cm)
    float Time;         // the ocean clock modulo VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP (s)
    float SpacingM;     // the mesh spacing (m; 0: no limit), for the height
    float FootprintM;   // the pixel's (m; 0: no limit), for the gradient
    float BedSlope;     // the bed's slope landward (m per m; at or below VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_KNOWN: unknown, Slope; stage O9b2)
    float BedDepthM;    // the terrain's own depth (m; 1e20 or more: unknown, DepthM), for the swash's foam (stage O9b2)
    float ForNormals;   // 1: the evaluation is for the normals (the footprint's rule for what the trains show), 0: the mesh's (stage O9b3)
};

struct FVoxelOceanSurf
{
    float Height;       // m, along the radial
    float Gradient;     // d height / d (distance landward), m per m: the gradient is this times e
    float Rate;         // d height / d t (m/s)
    float LongKeep;     // the long bands' amplitude factor (the handover)
    float Breaking;     // the bores' saturation (0 to 1)
    float Foam;         // the bores' and the swash's foam (0 to 1; stage O9b)
    float Active;
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurf VoxelOceanSurfNone()
{
    FVoxelOceanSurf S;
    S.Height = 0.0f;
    S.Gradient = 0.0f;
    S.Rate = 0.0f;
    S.LongKeep = 1.0f;
    S.Breaking = 0.0f;
    S.Foam = 0.0f;
    S.Active = 0.0f;
    return S;
}

// How far a wavelength is resolved at a spacing (VoxelOceanResolved's rule; 0: no limit).
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfResolved(float Wavelength, float Spacing)
{
    return Spacing > 0.0f ? saturate(Wavelength / (2.0f * Spacing) - 1.0f) : 1.0f;
}

// How far the mesh carries a wavelength at its spacing: fully from 8 spacings, nothing under 4 (a
// wave of 4 vertices a wavelength moving through the lattice reads as a sawtooth; 0: no limit).
VOXEL_FUNC float VoxelOceanSurfMeshResolved(float Wavelength, float Spacing)
{
    return Spacing > 0.0f ? saturate(Wavelength / (4.0f * Spacing) - 1.0f) : 1.0f;
}

// The swash's hold within its reach: the factor q on swings summing to A (m) for a limit of
// Limit (m; 0 none), and dq / dA.
VOXEL_FUNC float2 VoxelOceanSurfSwashHold(float A, float Limit)
{
    if (Limit <= 0.0f || A <= 0.0f) return float2(1.0f, 0.0f);
    const float X = A / Limit;
    const float U = X * X * X * X;
    const float Q = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrt(1.0f + U));
    const float Q2 = Q * Q;
    return float2(Q, -U * Q2 * Q2 * Q / A);
}

// One train at a point: its wave (d > 0) for the height (Spacing's front) and for the gradient
// (Footprint's), the shoreline's level, their derivatives.
struct FVoxelOceanSurfTrain
{
    float Wave;         // m (unweighed)
    float WaveRate;     // d wave / d t
    float WaveForSlope; // with the footprint's front
    float WaveDDepth;   // d (that) / d depth
    float Wavelength;   // the local wavelength (m)
    float Level;        // the shoreline's level (m)
    float LevelRate;
    float Setup;        // m
    float SetupRate;
    float Swing;        // the swash's mean half range (m; for the blend's width)
    float Saturation;   // H / (Index d)
    float Foam;         // the bore's foam at the point (0 to 1)
};

VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurfTrain VoxelOceanSurfTrainOf(int I, FVoxelOceanSurfInput In, FVoxelOceanSurfSettings S, float Hs, float HsRate, float Jitter,
    float GroupShift, float Agree, float Ground, float SwashSlope)
{
    FVoxelOceanSurfTrain Out;
    const float Cycles = VoxelOceanSurfCycles(I);
    const float Omega = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * Cycles / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP;
    const float K = Omega * Omega / VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_GRAVITY;
    const float M = In.Slope;
    const float Group = float(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_GROUP);
    const float GroupWeight = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_GROUP_WEIGHT * S.Sets;
    // The clock's phase and the groups' (exact across the wrap: Cycles is a multiple of GROUP).
    const float TimePhase = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * VoxelOceanSurfFrac(Cycles * In.Time / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP);
    const float GroupTime = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * VoxelOceanSurfFrac((Cycles / Group) * In.Time / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP);

    // The shoreline (Phi 0): Stockdon's setup and swings from the deep height (the groups' at the
    // shoreline for the incident swash), weighed by the field's agreement.
    const float Theta0 = TimePhase + Jitter;
    const float GroupPhase0 = VoxelOceanSurfAngle(GroupTime + Jitter / Group + GroupShift);
    const float GroupCos0 = cos(GroupPhase0);
    const float GroupSin0 = sin(GroupPhase0);
    const float GroupedShore = 1.0f + GroupWeight * GroupCos0;
    const float H0Shore = Hs * GroupedShore;
    const float DH0Shore = -Hs * GroupWeight * GroupSin0 * (Omega / Group) + HsRate * GroupedShore;
    const float L0 = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_GRAVITY / (Omega * Omega);
    // Stockdon's beach slope and the hold's: the bed's (stage O9b3; on a flat the swash hardly moves).
    const float Beta = min(SwashSlope, 0.1f);
    const float Weight = S.Swash * Agree;
    const float Root = sqrt(max(Hs * L0, 0.0f));
    const float RootShore = sqrt(max(H0Shore * L0, 0.0f));
    // Setup (Stockdon's mean).
    const float SetupStockdon = 0.35f * Beta * Root;
    const bool bSetup = SetupStockdon < 0.3f * Hs;
    Out.Setup = Weight * (bSetup ? SetupStockdon : 0.3f * Hs);
    Out.SetupRate = Weight * (bSetup ? 0.5f * SetupStockdon * HsRate / max(Hs, 1.0e-6f) : 0.3f * HsRate);
    // The incident swash, on each bore (a swing of the variance of Stockdon's).
    const float IncStockdon = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWING * 0.75f * Beta * RootShore;
    const bool bInc = IncStockdon < 0.5f * H0Shore;
    float SwingInc = Weight * (bInc ? IncStockdon : 0.5f * H0Shore);
    float DSwingInc = Weight * (bInc ? 0.5f * IncStockdon * DH0Shore / max(H0Shore, 1.0e-6f) : 0.5f * DH0Shore);
    // The infragravity swash, on the groups.
    const float IgStockdon = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWING * 0.06f * Root;
    const bool bIg = IgStockdon < 0.32f * Hs;
    float SwingIg = Weight * (bIg ? IgStockdon : 0.32f * Hs);
    float DSwingIg = Weight * (bIg ? 0.5f * IgStockdon * HsRate / max(Hs, 1.0e-6f) : 0.32f * HsRate);
    // Both held within the reach up and down the beach (at the field's slope).
    const float Limit = S.SwashReach * SwashSlope;
    const float SwingSum = SwingInc + SwingIg;
    const float2 Hold = VoxelOceanSurfSwashHold(SwingSum, Limit);
    const float DHold = Hold.y * (DSwingInc + DSwingIg);
    DSwingInc = Hold.x * DSwingInc + SwingInc * DHold;
    DSwingIg = Hold.x * DSwingIg + SwingIg * DHold;
    SwingInc *= Hold.x;
    SwingIg *= Hold.x;
    const FVoxelOceanSurfProfile Swash = VoxelOceanSurfProfileOf(Theta0 - VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWASH_LAG, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWASH_FRONT);
    Out.Level = Out.Setup + SwingInc * Swash.Shape + SwingIg * GroupCos0;
    Out.LevelRate = Out.SetupRate + SwingInc * Swash.DTheta * Omega + DSwingInc * Swash.Shape
        - SwingIg * GroupSin0 * (Omega / Group) + DSwingIg * GroupCos0;
    // The mean half range (the groups and the drift aside), held as the swings are.
    const float SwingMean = Weight * (min(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SWING * 0.75f * Beta * Root, 0.5f * Hs) + min(IgStockdon, 0.32f * Hs));
    Out.Swing = SwingMean * VoxelOceanSurfSwashHold(SwingMean, Limit).x;

    // The wave at the point (on the sea side).
    Out.Wave = 0.0f;
    Out.WaveRate = 0.0f;
    Out.WaveForSlope = 0.0f;
    Out.WaveDDepth = 0.0f;
    Out.Wavelength = L0;
    Out.Saturation = 0.0f;
    Out.Foam = 0.0f;
    const float D = In.DepthM;
    if (D > 0.0f)
    {
        const float Y = K * D;
        const FVoxelOceanDispersion Disp = VoxelOceanDispersionOf(Y);
        const float G = Y >= VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_DEEP ? 0.0f : 0.5f * VoxelOceanSinhIntegral(2.0f * Disp.X) - Disp.X * (1.0f - VoxelOceanShoalTanh(Disp.X));
        const float Phi = (Y + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_G0 - G) / M;
        const float LocalK = K * Disp.R;
        const float DPhi = LocalK / M;                      // d Phi / d depth
        const float Theta = Phi + TimePhase + Jitter;
        // The groups.
        const float GroupPhase = VoxelOceanSurfAngle(Phi / Group + GroupTime + Jitter / Group + GroupShift);
        const float GroupSin = sin(GroupPhase);
        const float Grouped = 1.0f + GroupWeight * cos(GroupPhase);
        // The height: shoaled, capped (Hc), with its derivatives in depth and time through the
        // groups and the cap (the gain's left out: it varies slowly).
        const float Gain = min(sqrt(Disp.R / (2.0f * Disp.N)), VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_MAX_GAIN);
        const float H0 = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_RMS * Hs;
        const float Raw = max(H0 * Grouped * Gain, 1.0e-6f);
        const float DRawDD = -H0 * Gain * GroupWeight * GroupSin * (DPhi / Group);
        const float DRawDT = -H0 * Gain * GroupWeight * GroupSin * (Omega / Group) + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_RMS * HsRate * Grouped * Gain;
        const float Index = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_INNER * S.Breaking;
        const float Cap = max(Index * D, 1.0e-6f);
        const float Ratio = Raw / Cap;
        const float R2 = Ratio * Ratio;
        const float Hc = Raw / sqrt(sqrt(1.0f + R2 * R2));
        const float QR = Hc / Raw;
        const float QC = Hc / Cap;
        const float QR2 = QR * QR;
        const float QC2 = QC * QC;
        const float DHcDD = QR2 * QR2 * QR * DRawDD + Index * QC2 * QC2 * QC;
        const float DHcDT = QR2 * QR2 * QR * DRawDT;
        // The front's share: the saturation's, held above what the spacing and the footprint resolve
        // of the wave's length on the ground.
        const float Wavelength = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI / LocalK * Ground;
        const float X = saturate((Ratio - 0.4f) / 0.6f);
        const float Sat = X * X * (3.0f - 2.0f * X);
        const bool bSat = Ratio > 0.4f && Ratio < 1.0f;
        const float DSat = bSat ? 6.0f * X * (1.0f - X) / 0.6f : 0.0f;
        const float Front = 0.5f * (1.0f - S.Skew * Sat);
        // d Ratio / d depth = DRaw / Cap - Ratio Index / Cap (the cap's own clamp aside).
        const float DFrontDD = bSat ? -0.5f * S.Skew * DSat * (DRawDD - Ratio * Index) / Cap : 0.0f;
        const float DFrontDT = bSat ? -0.5f * S.Skew * DSat * (DRawDT / Cap) : 0.0f;
        const float FrontH = max(Front, min(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MESH_FRONT * In.SpacingM / Wavelength, 0.5f));
        const float FrontN = max(Front, min(2.0f * In.FootprintM / Wavelength, 0.5f));
        const FVoxelOceanSurfProfile PH = VoxelOceanSurfProfileOf(Theta, FrontH);
        const FVoxelOceanSurfProfile PN = VoxelOceanSurfProfileOf(Theta, FrontN);
        Out.Wave = 0.5f * Hc * PH.Shape;
        Out.WaveRate = 0.5f * DHcDT * PH.Shape + 0.5f * Hc * (PH.DTheta * Omega + (FrontH > Front ? 0.0f : PH.DFront * DFrontDT));
        Out.WaveForSlope = 0.5f * Hc * PN.Shape;
        Out.WaveDDepth = 0.5f * DHcDD * PN.Shape + 0.5f * Hc * (PN.DTheta * DPhi + (FrontN > Front ? 0.0f : PN.DFront * DFrontDD));
        Out.Wavelength = Wavelength;
        Out.Saturation = Ratio;
        // The bore's foam: its face, the trail behind its crest (falling to nothing at the trough,
        // where the face's begins), a carpet (VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_TRAIL). Where the footprint
        // doesn't resolve the wave, its cycle's mean (no stripes).
        const float U = VoxelOceanSurfFrac(Theta * (1.0f / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI));
        const float Back = 1.0f - Front;
        const float Tail = exp(-Back * (1.0f / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_TRAIL));
        const float TrailScale = 1.0f / max(1.0f - Tail, 1.0e-6f);
        const float Face = U >= Back ? smoothstep(Back, 1.0f, U) : (exp(-U * (1.0f / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_TRAIL)) - Tail) * TrailScale;
        const float FaceMean = 0.5f * Front + (VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_TRAIL * (1.0f - Tail) - Back * Tail) * TrailScale;
        const float FaceSeen = FaceMean + (Face - FaceMean) * VoxelOceanSurfResolved(Wavelength, In.FootprintM);
        Out.Foam = Sat * saturate(0.25f + 0.75f * FaceSeen);
    }
    return Out;
}

// The surf at a point.
VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurf VoxelOceanSurfOf(FVoxelOceanSurfInput In, FVoxelOceanSurfSettings S)
{
    FVoxelOceanSurf Out = VoxelOceanSurfNone();
    if (S.Strength <= 0.0f || S.Breaking <= 0.0f || In.DepthM >= 1.0e20f || In.DepthM < -VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_LAND) return Out;
    const float Hs = In.Hs * S.Strength;
    if (Hs <= 1.0e-3f) return Out;
    const float D = In.DepthM;
    // The handover's depth: Handover breaking depths of the significant height, past the blend
    // into the swash's level (2 m at most) at least.
    const float Reach = max(S.Handover * Hs / S.Breaking, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MIN_REACH);
    if (D >= Reach) return Out;
    // The swash's level fades out inland by the field's distance, on both sides of the still
    // level (stage O9b3: on land alone it left a step at every point that crosses it).
    const float Inland = 1.0f - smoothstep(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_INLAND, 2.0f * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_INLAND, -In.ShoreM);
    if (Inland <= 0.0f && D <= 0.0f) return Out;
    const float Agree = saturate(In.Agree);
    // The bed: its slope (the field's where unknown), the waves' length on the ground against
    // their local wavelength, and where the trains hold (stage O9b2).
    const float Bed = In.BedSlope > VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_KNOWN ? clamp(In.BedSlope, -VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_MAX, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_MAX) : In.Slope;
    const float BedHeld = max(Bed, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_FADE0 * In.Slope);
    const float Ground = In.Slope / BedHeld;
    const float Valid = smoothstep(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_FADE0, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_BED_FADE1, Bed / In.Slope);
    // The trains' amplitude (C1 at the handover's edge) and its derivative in depth; the long
    // bands keep the rest of the energy.
    const float ShareX = saturate((D - 0.4f * Reach) / (0.6f * Reach));
    const float Handed = (1.0f - ShareX * ShareX * (3.0f - 2.0f * ShareX)) * Agree;
    // The trains' share: what the handover took, where the bed holds them.
    const float Share = Handed * Valid;
    const float DShare = D > 0.4f * Reach ? -6.0f * ShareX * (1.0f - ShareX) / (0.6f * Reach) * Agree * Valid : 0.0f;
    Out.Active = 1.0f;

    // The two trains around the sea state's peak period, sharing its energy.
    const float Period = clamp(VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PERIOD_PER_SPEED * max(In.Speed, 3.0f), VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MIN_PERIOD, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MAX_PERIOD);
    int Lower = 0;
    for (int T = 0; T < VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TRAINS - 1; T++)
    {
        if (VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP / VoxelOceanSurfCycles(T) <= Period) Lower = T;
    }
    Lower = min(Lower, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TRAINS - 2);
    const float TLow = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP / VoxelOceanSurfCycles(Lower);
    const float THigh = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_WRAP / VoxelOceanSurfCycles(Lower + 1);
    const float Upper = saturate(log2(Period / TLow) / log2(THigh / TLow));
    const float AmpA = cos(0.5f * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI * Upper);
    const float AmpB = sin(0.5f * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_PI * Upper);
    const float WA = AmpA * AmpA;
    const float WB = AmpB * AmpB;

    // The sets' noises (cells of 40, 10 and 15 units: 1.6 km, 410 m, 610 m).
    const float GroupShift = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * VoxelOceanSurfNoise2(In.Units, In.Low, 40, 0x51u, 0x2c9u).x;
    const float2 Drift = VoxelOceanSurfNoiseTime(In.Units, In.Low, 10, In.Time * (1.0f / 120.0f), 30u, 0x7a3u);
    const float Jitter = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_TWO_PI * S.Sets * (VoxelOceanSurfNoise2(In.Units, In.Low, 15, 0x2c9u, 0x51u).x - 0.5f);
    const float Height = Hs * (1.0f + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRIFT * S.Sets * (2.0f * Drift.x - 1.0f));
    const float HeightRate = Hs * 2.0f * VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRIFT * S.Sets * Drift.y * (1.0f / 120.0f);

    const FVoxelOceanSurfTrain A = VoxelOceanSurfTrainOf(Lower, In, S, Height, HeightRate, Jitter, GroupShift, Agree, Ground, BedHeld);
    const FVoxelOceanSurfTrain B = VoxelOceanSurfTrainOf(Lower + 1, In, S, Height, HeightRate, Jitter, GroupShift, Agree, Ground, BedHeld);
    // The long bands keep what the trains don't show (stage O9b3): the handover's share where the
    // bed holds the trains and the mesh resolves them (by energy). Where they can't be shown (too
    // short for the mesh or the footprint, a flat or a bar's back) the long bands carry the waves:
    // a wave is always drawn by one or the other.
    // The trains' shown energy: the mesh's rule for the height, the footprint's for the normals.
    const float RA = In.ForNormals > 0.5f ? VoxelOceanSurfResolved(A.Wavelength, In.FootprintM) : VoxelOceanSurfMeshResolved(A.Wavelength, In.SpacingM);
    const float RB = In.ForNormals > 0.5f ? VoxelOceanSurfResolved(B.Wavelength, In.FootprintM) : VoxelOceanSurfMeshResolved(B.Wavelength, In.SpacingM);
    const float Taken2 = Share * Share * (WA * RA * RA + WB * RB * RB);
    Out.LongKeep = sqrt(max(1.0f - Taken2, 0.0f));
    // The swash's sheet on land reaches only so far up the beach (stage O9b3): its distance from
    // the still waterline, the ground's height over the bed's slope, held within 1.5 to 3 times
    // the reach. On a plain near sea level the flat sheet would cover all ground below its level.
    const float UpBeach = D < 0.0f ? -D / BedHeld : 0.0f;
    float Sheet = 1.0f;
    float DSheet = 0.0f;    // d Sheet / d(landward)
    if (S.SwashReach > 0.0f)
    {
        const float S0 = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SHEET0 * S.SwashReach;
        const float S1 = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_SHEET1 * S.SwashReach;
        const float SX = saturate((UpBeach - S0) / (S1 - S0));
        Sheet = 1.0f - SX * SX * (3.0f - 2.0f * SX);
        // Up the beach grows landward by the bed's slope over the held slope.
        DSheet = D < 0.0f && UpBeach > S0 && UpBeach < S1 ? -6.0f * SX * (1.0f - SX) / (S1 - S0) * (Bed / BedHeld) : 0.0f;
    }
    // Energy: the waves add by amplitude (cos, sin), the levels by energy.
    const float LevelHere = (WA * A.Level + WB * B.Level) * Inland;
    const float Level = LevelHere * Sheet;
    const float LevelRate = (WA * A.LevelRate + WB * B.LevelRate) * Inland * Sheet;
    const float Setup = WA * A.Setup + WB * B.Setup;
    const float SetupRate = WA * A.SetupRate + WB * B.SetupRate;
    const float Swing = WA * A.Swing + WB * B.Swing;
    Out.Breaking = saturate(WA * A.Saturation + WB * B.Saturation) * Share;
    // The swash's foam: where its sheet runs thin (the level less the terrain's own bed, so the
    // foamy edge follows the visible waterline), a fifth elsewhere.
    const float Thickness = max(Level + (In.BedDepthM < 1.0e20f ? In.BedDepthM : D), 0.0f);
    const float SwashFoam = S.Foam * Agree * Inland * Sheet * (0.2f + 0.8f * exp(-Thickness * (1.0f / VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_FOAM_THIN)));

    if (D <= 0.0f)
    {
        // Above the still level: the shoreline's level, flat (up the beach as far as it reaches).
        Out.Height = Level;
        Out.Rate = LevelRate;
        Out.Foam = saturate(SwashFoam);
        Out.Gradient = LevelHere * DSheet;
        return Out;
    }
    // The sea's surface: the trains' waves (weighed by how the spacing resolves them) and the surf
    // zone's setup (from the shoreline's out to the breaking depth of the significant height).
    const float HeightA = VoxelOceanSurfMeshResolved(A.Wavelength, In.SpacingM) * AmpA * Share;
    const float HeightB = VoxelOceanSurfMeshResolved(B.Wavelength, In.SpacingM) * AmpB * Share;
    const float NormalA = VoxelOceanSurfResolved(A.Wavelength, In.FootprintM) * AmpA;
    const float NormalB = VoxelOceanSurfResolved(B.Wavelength, In.FootprintM) * AmpB;
    const float BreakDepth = max(Hs / S.Breaking, 0.1f);
    const float SetupX = saturate(D / BreakDepth);
    const float SetupShape = 1.0f - SetupX * SetupX * (3.0f - 2.0f * SetupX);
    const float SetupHere = Setup * SetupShape;
    const float DSetup = D < BreakDepth ? -Setup * 6.0f * SetupX * (1.0f - SetupX) / BreakDepth : 0.0f;
    const float Sea = HeightA * A.Wave + HeightB * B.Wave + SetupHere;
    const float SeaRate = HeightA * A.WaveRate + HeightB * B.WaveRate + SetupRate * SetupShape;
    const float WavesForSlope = NormalA * A.WaveForSlope + NormalB * B.WaveForSlope;
    const float SeaForSlope = Share * WavesForSlope + SetupHere;
    const float DSea = Share * (NormalA * A.WaveDDepth + NormalB * B.WaveDDepth) + DShare * WavesForSlope + DSetup;
    // Into the shoreline's level within Dsw of depth: half the waves' wavelength at the swash's
    // depth, along the beach (so the last bore runs into it), within 1.5 times the swash's range
    // and 2 m. Constant in time (the mean swash), so the blend has no rate of its own.
    const float SwashDepth = max(Setup + Swing, 0.1f);
    const float Dsw = clamp(0.5f * BedHeld * Period * sqrt(VOXEL_OCEAN_SHOAL_GRAVITY * SwashDepth), 0.02f, min(1.5f * SwashDepth, VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_MIN_REACH));
    const float X = saturate(D / Dsw);
    const float Blend = X * X * (3.0f - 2.0f * X);
    const float DBlend = D < Dsw ? 6.0f * X * (1.0f - X) / Dsw : 0.0f;
    Out.Height = Level + (Sea - Level) * Blend;
    Out.Rate = LevelRate + (SeaRate - LevelRate) * Blend;
    // The bores' foam (by energy) on the sea's side, the swash's within its blend.
    const float BoreFoam = S.Foam * Share * (WA * A.Foam + WB * B.Foam);
    Out.Foam = saturate(SwashFoam + (BoreFoam - SwashFoam) * Blend);
    // Landward the depth falls by the bed's slope: d / d(landward) = -b d / d depth.
    Out.Gradient = -Bed * ((SeaForSlope - Level) * DBlend + DSea * Blend);
    return Out;
}

// THE DRAIN (stage O9b3): an inland basin below sea level (the shore field's distance under minus
// the margin, not joined to the sea) is dry, and the sea that reaches toward it across low ground
// within the margin used to end there in mid-air: a wall of water where the ground is below sea
// level on both sides. From the bake's margin (DRAIN_START of the basins' margin, the cull's: the
// bake's coast can sit a cell from the terrain's, so the sea is kept whole out to the bake's
// margin) to the basins' margin inland (by the field) the sea's surface sinks below the bottom (to
// DRAIN_DEPTH under the depth the waves feel) and its waves die out, so it meets the terrain
// instead. Every evaluation applies it alike (the mesh, the underwater pass, the query): Keep
// scales the waves (their slope variance by Keep^2), Drop (m) lowers the surface, Slope is the
// drop's rise landward (m per m, along the field's direction; the gradient's change is minus it).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRAIN_DEPTH 3.0f
// The drain's start, as a share of the basins' margin (1 / VoxelOceanWaves::BasinDrainSpan).
#define VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRAIN_START 0.6666667f

struct FVoxelOceanSurfDrain
{
    float Keep;
    float Drop;
    float Slope;
};

// ShoreM the field's distance (m, minus inland; 1e20 or more: no field), DepthM the depth the
// waves feel (m; 1e20 or more unknown), Bed the depth's fall landward (m per m), MarginM the
// basins' margin (m; 0: no drain).
VOXEL_FUNC FVoxelOceanSurfDrain VoxelOceanSurfDrainOf(float ShoreM, float DepthM, float Bed, float MarginM)
{
    FVoxelOceanSurfDrain D;
    D.Keep = 1.0f;
    D.Drop = 0.0f;
    D.Slope = 0.0f;
    if (MarginM <= 0.0f || ShoreM >= 1.0e20f) return D;
    const float Start = VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRAIN_START * MarginM;
    const float X = saturate((-ShoreM - Start) / (MarginM - Start));
    const float W = X * X * (3.0f - 2.0f * X);
    const float Depth = DepthM < 1.0e20f ? DepthM : 0.0f;
    D.Keep = 1.0f - W;
    D.Drop = W * (max(Depth, 0.0f) + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRAIN_DEPTH);
    // Landward the field's distance falls one for one and the depth by the bed's slope.
    const float DW = X > 0.0f && X < 1.0f ? 6.0f * X * (1.0f - X) / (MarginM - Start) : 0.0f;
    D.Slope = DW * (max(Depth, 0.0f) + VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_DRAIN_DEPTH) - (Depth > 0.0f ? W * Bed : 0.0f);
    return D;
}

#endif // VOXEL_OCEAN_SURF_USH
